---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../../styles/docs.css";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const image = (name: string) => `${base}images/guides/${name}.png`;
---

<Base
	title="Transaction Inspector | Actual Budget Tweaks"
	description="See a transaction's payee history, rules and schedule in a side panel."
>
	<main class="docs center">
		<header class="docs__header stack stack--sm">
			<a href="/guides" class="docs__back">Back to guides</a>
			<h1>Transaction Inspector</h1>
			<p class="docs__lead">
				Transaction Inspector shows a transaction's payee history, rules and schedule in a side panel.
				Use it to check a charge or find out why a transaction got its category.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Inspecting a transaction</h2>
			<p>Turn on Transaction Inspector in the Features section of Tweaks, then:</p>
			<ol>
				<li>Open an account and click <strong>Inspect</strong> in its toolbar.</li>
				<li>Tick a transaction's checkbox.</li>
			</ol>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Reading the panel</h2>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={image("inspector")}
					width="340"
					height="711"
					alt="The Inspector panel for a City Power bill marked 28% above usual, with its payee history, the Power bill schedule and two rules"
				/>
			</div>
			<ul>
				<li>A badge like <strong>+28% vs usual</strong> means the amount is at least 25% away from the payee's average. It's a prompt to check the charge, and it needs three or more transactions from that payee.</li>
				<li><strong>Payee history</strong> shows the payee's average amount and recent transactions.</li>
				<li><strong>Schedule</strong> shows the linked schedule and its next date.</li>
				<li><strong>Rules for this payee</strong> lists each rule in plain words. Click the pencil to edit one.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Finding a transaction that doesn't match your rules</h2>
			<div class="docs__stage docs__stage--card">
				<img
					src={image("inspector-rules")}
					width="340"
					height="420"
					alt="The Inspector panel for a Fuel Stop charge, warning that rules would change its category from Fun to Transport"
				/>
			</div>
			<p><strong>Your rules would change</strong> appears when your rules would now give the transaction a different result.</p>
			<p>This usually means it was edited by hand or added before the rule existed. The panel doesn't change the transaction.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="docs__section">
			<h2>Creating a rule</h2>
			<p><strong>Create rule from this</strong> opens Actual's rule editor with the payee and category filled in.</p>
		</section>
	</main>
</Base>
